# Cursor Hooks

Hooks are optional automation around agent events. Keep them project-local,
fast, deterministic, and scoped to changed files.

- A hook must not install dependencies, mutate unrelated files, read the raw
  dataset, publish artifacts, deploy, or bypass permissions.
- Prefer repository-owned Bun/Nx/Biome commands after those tools exist.
- Do not make every edit trigger a global build or full test suite.
- Treat hook input as untrusted and quote file paths safely.
- Keep final risk-based QA explicit rather than hiding it in a session-stop
  hook.
